IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `fhog-terms`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`

-- Stamp Duties Act 1923 (SA) -- conveyance duty on a home, the relief on a new home or land to build on, its loss, and
-- the foreign ownership surcharge. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE: the rules are in the Act's own actors and terms ("the purchasers
-- under the contract", "the person who executed the instrument", "the Commissioner"). The buyer's questions are in
-- sda-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module and restates no rule.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- through the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0). The deposited text is AS AT 2025-02-13 (scraped 2025-03-10), at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/stamp-duties-act-1923.txt. Not the official text; it may be out of date. The duty scale
-- is encoded as the deposited text states it. Nine formulas are missing from the deposit
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/stamp-duties-act-1923.formulas.md); two of them, s 71DD(7)(a) and (b), would set the
-- relief on a pre-6 June 2024 contract in the phase-out band, which therefore answers `not covered`.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 2 (spouse, domestic partner, foreign person for a natural person (s 2(14)(a)(i))); s 20(1),
-- (2), (4)-(7) (pay and stamp within 2 months, regulative; the $10 000 offence); s 60A(1), (2) (value of the property
-- conveyed); Schedule 2 clause 3(1)(b) (the general scale, nine bands, as a table); s 71CB (transfers of a shared
-- residence, or of a vehicle's registration, between spouses or domestic partners, current or former); s 71DD(1)-(3),
-- (6), (8), (9), (11), (11a), (12), (13) (relief on a new home or vacant land to build on); s 71DD(9a) (the
-- Commissioner's determination an INPUT; the original contract's relief it gives answers `not covered`); s 71DB(1)
-- and the s 71DB(7) dates of a qualifying off-the-plan contract (where s 71DB applies the duty answers `not covered`);
-- s 71DD(4), (5) (the
-- residence requirement, regulative, with the Commissioner's shorter period, longer completion period or exemption of
-- a co-purchaser as INPUTS) with s 71DE (duty at the transfer date's rates, chargeable for s 20(2), interest and penalty
-- tax under the Taxation Administration Act Part 5 at the Commissioner's discretion); s 72(1)-(5), (8) (the 7% foreign
-- ownership surcharge and its refund, regulative), with s 71DD(11a) and s 72(4) (the relief and the surcharge).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the s 71DB concessions themselves (off-the-plan apartments; the s 71DB(3)(a) DV formula is missing),
-- s 71DD(7) (formula missing), the relief a s 71DD(9a) determination carries over, s 72(6), (7) (trusts; becoming a foreign person later), landholder duty (Part 4), ss 71C-71CC, 71CBA, 71D-71DC,
-- 71E-71F, s 60A(3)-(9) (valuations and anti-avoidance), and the general exemptions of Schedule 2 Part 2.
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Stamp Duties Act 1923 -- conveyance duty on a home, seat-neutral core`

§§ `s 60A -- value of the property conveyed`

-- s 60A(1): "a reference in this Act ... to the value of property conveyed or transferred is a reference to the market
-- value of the property as at the date of the conveyance, assuming that the property had, at that date, been free from
-- any encumbrances." (2): "In the case of a conveyance on sale, the Commissioner may treat the consideration for the sale
-- as being the value of the property ... unless it appears to the Commissioner that the consideration may be less than
-- the value of the property as referred to in subsection (1)." The market value is a valuation (an INPUT); whether the
-- Commissioner takes the price is the Commissioner's choice (a fact), open only on a sale.
GIVEN `the market value, free of encumbrances, at the date of the conveyance` IS A NUMBER
      `the consideration for the sale` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a conveyance on sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner treats the consideration as the value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the property conveyed (s 60A)` MEANS
    IF `it is a conveyance on sale` AND `the Commissioner treats the consideration as the value`
    THEN `the consideration for the sale`
    ELSE `the market value, free of encumbrances, at the date of the conveyance`

§§ `Schedule 2 clause 3(1)(b) -- the general scale, as a table`

-- Schedule 2 clause 3(1): "Conveyance or transfer on sale of any property (not otherwise charged), including contract or
-- agreement for sale, or conveyance operating as a voluntary disposition inter vivos of any property ... (b) where the
-- value of the property conveyed --
--   (i)    does not exceed $12 000 -- for every $100 or fractional part of $100 of the value          $1.00
--   (ii)   exceeds $12 000 but does not exceed $30 000    $120 plus $2.00 for every $100 or part of the excess over $12 000
--   (iii)  exceeds $30 000 but does not exceed $50 000    $480 plus $3.00 ... over $30 000
--   (iv)   exceeds $50 000 but does not exceed $100 000   $1 080 plus $3.50 ... over $50 000
--   (v)    exceeds $100 000 but does not exceed $200 000  $2 830 plus $4.00 ... over $100 000
--   (vi)   exceeds $200 000 but does not exceed $250 000  $6 830 plus $4.25 ... over $200 000
--   (vii)  exceeds $250 000 but does not exceed $300 000  $8 955 plus $4.75 ... over $250 000
--   (viii) exceeds $300 000 but does not exceed $500 000  $11 330 plus $5.00 ... over $300 000
--   (ix)   exceeds $500 000                                $21 330 plus $5.50 ... over $500 000"
-- A band: on a value above `above`, the duty is `base amount` plus `per 100` for each $100 or part of the excess. Each
-- base is the duty at the top of the band below, so the scale is continuous (asserted in the cases).
DECLARE `Rate band` HAS
    `above`       IS A NUMBER
    `base amount` IS A NUMBER
    `per 100`     IS A NUMBER

-- The table, highest band first: the first band whose floor the value exceeds is the one that applies.
`the general scale (Schedule 2 clause 3(1)(b))` MEANS
    LIST `Rate band` OF 500000, 21330, 5.50
         `Rate band` OF 300000, 11330, 5.00
         `Rate band` OF 250000, 8955, 4.75
         `Rate band` OF 200000, 6830, 4.25
         `Rate band` OF 100000, 2830, 4.00
         `Rate band` OF 50000, 1080, 3.50
         `Rate band` OF 30000, 480, 3.00
         `Rate band` OF 12000, 120, 2.00
         `Rate band` OF 0, 0, 1.00

GIVEN `scale` IS A LIST OF `Rate band`
      `the value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty on the scale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `scale`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `band` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `the value` GREATER THAN `band`'s `above`
        THEN `band`'s `base amount`
             PLUS (`band`'s `per 100` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the value` MINUS `band`'s `above`))
        ELSE `the duty on the scale` `rest` `the value`

GIVEN `the value of the property conveyed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the conveyance duty on the general scale` MEANS
    `the duty on the scale` `the general scale (Schedule 2 clause 3(1)(b))` `the value of the property conveyed`

§§ `s 20 -- time for payment of duty and stamping (regulative)`

-- s 20(1): "Subject to any express provision to the contrary, if an instrument is chargeable with duty, the duty must be
-- paid and the instrument stamped -- (a) in the case of an instrument executed in South Australia -- within two months
-- after its execution; or (b) in the case of an instrument executed outside South Australia -- within two months after
-- its receipt in South Australia or within six months after its execution, whichever period first expires."
DECLARE `Where the instrument was executed` IS ONE OF
    `in South Australia`
    `outside South Australia` HAS `the date it was received in South Australia` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the date of execution` IS A DATE
      `where` IS A `Where the instrument was executed`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay the duty and stamp the instrument (s 20(1))` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where`
    WHEN `in South Australia` THEN `months after` 2 `the date of execution`
    WHEN `outside South Australia` `received` THEN
        `the earlier of` (`months after` 2 `received`) `and` (`months after` 6 `the date of execution`)

-- s 20(2): "If duty or further duty becomes chargeable on an instrument in consequence of an event occurring after its
-- execution, the duty must be paid and the instrument stamped within two months after that event." s 71DE(2)(e) makes
-- the loss of the s 71DD relief such an event.
GIVEN `the date of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay duty that becomes chargeable after execution (s 20(2))` MEANS
    `months after` 2 `the date of the event`

-- s 20(4): "If an instrument that is chargeable with stamp duty is not produced to the Commissioner for stamping within the
-- period prescribed by this section, any person who executed the instrument, or on whose behalf it was executed, is
-- guilty of an offence. Maximum penalty: $10 000." (5): not if "duly stamped in some other manner authorised by this Act
-- within the relevant period". (6): "It is a defence ... to prove that the defendant delivered the instrument or had it
-- delivered into the possession of some other party, or an agent for some other party, to the instrument in the
-- reasonable expectation that the other party would have it stamped." (7): the offence "does not affect the validity of
-- the instrument".
`the maximum penalty for not stamping in time (s 20(4))` MEANS 10000

GIVEN `it was produced for stamping within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was duly stamped in another authorised manner within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was delivered to another party in the reasonable expectation that they would have it stamped` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the person who executed it can be fined (s 20(4)-(6))` MEANS
    IF     `it was produced for stamping within the period`
        OR `it was duly stamped in another authorised manner within the period`
        OR `it was delivered to another party in the reasonable expectation that they would have it stamped`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the maximum penalty for not stamping in time (s 20(4))`

-- The rule. Clock: days from execution (or from the s 20(2) event). `the days allowed` is the count of days to the s 20
-- last day, from the dates above. An instrument not chargeable with duty has no s 20 obligation.
GIVEN `the instrument is chargeable with duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 20 -- pay the duty and have the instrument stamped within the period` IS
    IF `the instrument is chargeable with duty`
    THEN PARTY  `the person who executed the instrument`
         MUST   `pay the duty and have the instrument stamped`
         WITHIN `the days allowed`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the person who executed the instrument` BECAUSE "s 20(1), (4): the duty must be paid and the instrument stamped within two months after execution (or the s 20(1)(b) period); not produced in time, an offence with a maximum penalty of $10 000, and a tax default with interest and penalty tax under Taxation Administration Act Part 5"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `s 2 -- spouse and domestic partner (Stamp Duties Act)`

-- s 2(1): "spouse -- a person is the spouse of another if they are legally married"; "domestic partner means a person who
-- is a domestic partner within the meaning of the Family Relationships Act 1975, whether declared as such under that
-- Act or not" -- a borrowed term, a FACT. s 71DD(11): "If the Commissioner is satisfied that, at the time of deciding an
-- application under this section, an applicant -- (a) is legally married but not cohabiting with the person to whom the
-- applicant is legally married; and (b) has no intention of resuming cohabitation, the person to whom the applicant is
-- legally married is not to be regarded as the applicant's spouse."
GIVEN `they are legally married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they cohabit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant intends to resume cohabitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person counts as the applicant's spouse for s 71DD` IF
        `they are legally married`
    AND (`they cohabit` OR `the applicant intends to resume cohabitation`)

§§ `s 71CB -- transfers between spouses or domestic partners, current or former`

-- s 71CB(1): "shared residence means -- (a) in relation to spouses or domestic partners -- their principal place of
-- residence of which both or either of them is owner; (b) in relation to former spouses or domestic partners -- their last
-- principal place of residence of which both or either of them was owner, but does not include premises that form part
-- of industrial or commercial premises."
GIVEN `it is (or was last) their principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both or either of them is (or was) owner of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it forms part of industrial or commercial premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises are a shared residence (s 71CB(1))` IF
        `it is (or was last) their principal place of residence`
    AND `both or either of them is (or was) owner of it`
    AND (NOT `it forms part of industrial or commercial premises`)

DECLARE `Relationship of the parties` IS ONE OF
    `spouses or domestic partners`
    `former spouses or former domestic partners`
    `neither`

-- s 71CB(2): "an instrument of which the sole effect is -- (a) to transfer -- (i) an interest in a shared residence; or
-- (ii) registration of a motor vehicle, between parties who are spouses or former spouses, or domestic partners or former
-- domestic partners; or (b) to register a motor vehicle in the name of a person whose spouse or former spouse, or
-- domestic partner or former domestic partner, was the last registered owner of the vehicle ..., is exempt from stamp
-- duty." (3): between former spouses or partners only "if the Commissioner is satisfied that the instrument has been
-- executed as a result of the irretrievable breakdown of the parties' marriage or relationship" (a fact). (4): duty paid
-- because the Commissioner was not then satisfied is refunded if later satisfied.
GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `Relationship of the parties`
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it results from the irretrievable breakdown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parties qualify under s 71CB(2), (3)` IF
    CONSIDER `the relationship`
    WHEN `spouses or domestic partners` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `former spouses or former domestic partners` THEN `the Commissioner is satisfied it results from the irretrievable breakdown`
    WHEN `neither` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `its sole effect is to transfer an interest in the premises between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises are a shared residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship` IS A `Relationship of the parties`
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it results from the irretrievable breakdown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer of the home is exempt (s 71CB(2)(a)(i))` IF
        `its sole effect is to transfer an interest in the premises between the parties`
    AND `the premises are a shared residence`
    AND `the parties qualify under s 71CB(2), (3)` `the relationship` `the Commissioner is satisfied it results from the irretrievable breakdown`

GIVEN `its sole effect is to transfer the registration between the parties, or to register it in the name of the last owner's partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship` IS A `Relationship of the parties`
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it results from the irretrievable breakdown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle application is exempt (s 71CB(2)(a)(ii), (b))` IF
        `its sole effect is to transfer the registration between the parties, or to register it in the name of the last owner's partner`
    AND `the parties qualify under s 71CB(2), (3)` `the relationship` `the Commissioner is satisfied it results from the irretrievable breakdown`

§§ `s 71DD -- relief on a new home or vacant land on which a home is to be built`

-- s 71DD(1): the section applies if, on an application, the Commissioner is satisfied that "(a) the applicant is a
-- purchaser under a contract for the conveyance or transfer of a new home or vacant land on which a home is to be built;
-- and (b) the conveyance or transfer qualifies for relief under this section". (13): "home" and "new home" have the FHOG
-- Act's meanings (fhog-terms.l4: `the building is a home (s 4)`, `the home is a new home (s 3)`).
DECLARE `What is bought` IS ONE OF
    `a new home`
    `vacant land on which a home is to be built`
    `something else`

-- The facts of one contract (the text's natural unit). "the Commissioner is satisfied" is answered conditionally, as a
-- fact. "a purchaser or spouse" covers every purchaser and every spouse or domestic partner of one (s 71DD(11): a
-- separated spouse does not count). "the commencement date of the contract" (s 71DD(3)(e)) is not defined in the Act:
-- READING (NOTES.md, finding 6) it is the date the contract was entered into. "Australian citizen" and "permanent
-- resident" (s 71DD(13)) are Commonwealth terms, FACTS. "relevant interest" is the FHOG Act's (s 71DD(12)), asked as a
-- fact here (fhog-terms.l4 works it out for one interest).
DECLARE `New home purchase` HAS
    `what is bought`                                                                   IS A `What is bought`
    `the date the contract was entered into`                                           IS A DATE
    `the market value when the contract was entered into`                              IS A NUMBER
    `every purchaser is at least 18, or the Commissioner so determines under s 71DD(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least one purchaser is an Australian citizen or permanent resident when applying` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a purchaser or spouse was a party to an earlier conveyance relieved under s 71DD(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a purchaser or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in SA or another State before the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a purchaser or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant day`                                                                 IS A DATE
    `every applicant is a natural person`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `every owner after the transfer joins in the application`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner determines under s 71DD(9a) that the contract has the original contract's relief` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "the relevant day" (s 71DD(13)): "the day on which the Statutes Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2025 is assented to by
-- the Governor" -- not in the operative text, so an INPUT (NOTES.md, finding 3).
`the first day of the relief (s 71DD(3)(a))` MEANS YearMonthDay 2023 6 15
`the day the relief became nil duty at any value (s 71DD(2)(b))` MEANS YearMonthDay 2024 6 6

-- s 71DD(3)(f): "if the contract ... was entered into before 6 June 2024, the market value of the new home (including the
-- land on which the home is situated) or vacant land when the contract is entered into is less than -- (i) in the case
-- of a new home -- $700 000; and (ii) in the case of vacant land on which a home is to be built -- $450 000."
GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pre-6 June 2024 value cap is met (s 71DD(3)(f))` IF
    IF (`p`'s `the date the contract was entered into`) `is on or after` `the day the relief became nil duty at any value (s 71DD(2)(b))`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `p`'s `what is bought`
         WHEN `a new home` THEN `p`'s `the market value when the contract was entered into` LESS THAN 700000
         WHEN `vacant land on which a home is to be built` THEN `p`'s `the market value when the contract was entered into` LESS THAN 450000
         WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE

-- s 71DD(3): "A conveyance or transfer of a new home, or of vacant land on which a home is to be built, qualifies for
-- relief under this section if -- (a) the contract ... was entered into on or after 15 June 2023; and (b) subject to
-- subsection (6), the purchasers under the contract are at least 18 years of age; and (c) at least 1 of the purchasers
-- under the contract is an Australian citizen or permanent resident at the time application for the benefit of this
-- section is made; and (d) no purchaser under the contract, and no spouse or domestic partner of a purchaser under the
-- contract, has been a party to an earlier conveyance or transfer for which no duty, or a reduced rate of duty, was
-- payable under subsection (2); and (e) no purchaser ..., and no spouse or domestic partner of a purchaser ..., has,
-- before the commencement date of the contract -- (i) held a relevant interest in residential property in South
-- Australia or another State; and (ii) if the commencement date of the contract is before the relevant day, occupied the
-- property as a place of residence for a continuous period of at least 6 months; and (f) [the cap above]".
GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` IF
        (CONSIDER `p`'s `what is bought`
         WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND ((`p`'s `the date the contract was entered into`) `is on or after` `the first day of the relief (s 71DD(3)(a))`)
    AND `p`'s `every purchaser is at least 18, or the Commissioner so determines under s 71DD(6)`
    AND `p`'s `at least one purchaser is an Australian citizen or permanent resident when applying`
    AND (NOT (`p`'s `a purchaser or spouse was a party to an earlier conveyance relieved under s 71DD(2)`))
    AND (NOT (    `p`'s `a purchaser or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in SA or another State before the contract`
              AND (   ((`p`'s `the date the contract was entered into`) `is on or after` (`p`'s `the relevant day`))
                   OR `p`'s `a purchaser or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months`)))
    AND `the pre-6 June 2024 value cap is met (s 71DD(3)(f))` `p`

-- s 71DD(8): "An application under subsection (1) -- (a) may only be made by a natural person; and (b) must be made
-- jointly by each person who is, or will be, following the conveyance or transfer ..., an owner of the relevant new home
-- or vacant land". (9): the section "does not apply to a contract ... if the Commissioner is satisfied that the relevant
-- contract replaces a contract entered into -- (a) if the relevant contract was entered into before 6 June 2024 -- before
-- 15 June 2023; or (b) if ... on or after 6 June 2024 -- before 6 June 2024, for the conveyance or transfer of the same new
-- home or vacant land" (the fact names the right earlier date). (9) is "Subject to subsection (9a)": see below.
GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 71DD applies to the conveyance (s 71DD(1), (8), (9))` IF
        `the conveyance qualifies for relief (s 71DD(3))` `p`
    AND `p`'s `every applicant is a natural person`
    AND `p`'s `every owner after the transfer joins in the application`
    AND (NOT (`p`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land`))

-- s 71DD(9a): "Despite subsection (9)(b), if the Commissioner is satisfied that a contract entered into on or after
-- 6 June 2024 (the prescribed relevant contract) replaces a contract entered into before 6 June 2024 (the original
-- contract) for the conveyance or transfer of the same new home or vacant land, the Commissioner may determine that the
-- conveyance or transfer under the prescribed relevant contract qualifies for the relief that the conveyance or transfer
-- under the original contract would have qualified for under this section if the prescribed relevant contract had not
-- replaced the original contract." The determination is the Commissioner's discretion (an INPUT). Without it, (9)(b)
-- bars the relief. With it, the relief is the original contract's, which turns on that contract's date, market value
-- and purchasers (s 71DD(2)(a), (3)) -- facts this encoding does not take, so the duty answers `not covered`. The
-- application is still one under s 71DD(1), so (8) applies to it.
GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 71DD(9a) gives the conveyance the original contract's relief` IF
        ((`p`'s `the date the contract was entered into`) `is on or after` `the day the relief became nil duty at any value (s 71DD(2)(b))`)
    AND `p`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land`
    AND `p`'s `the Commissioner determines under s 71DD(9a) that the contract has the original contract's relief`
    AND `p`'s `every applicant is a natural person`
    AND `p`'s `every owner after the transfer joins in the application`

-- s 71DD(2): "(a) if the contract ... was entered into before 6 June 2024 -- (i) ... a new home where the market value of
-- the home (including the land on which the home is situated) when the contract is entered into does not exceed
-- $650 000 -- no duty will be payable; or (ii) ... exceeds $650 000 but is less than $700 000 -- the duty otherwise
-- payable will be reduced in accordance with subsection (7); or (iii) ... vacant land where the market value of the land
-- ... does not exceed $400 000 -- no duty will be payable; or (iv) ... exceeds $400 000 but is less than $450 000 -- the
-- duty otherwise payable will be reduced in accordance with subsection (7); (b) if the contract ... was entered into on or
-- after 6 June 2024 -- no duty will be payable." The (7) formulas are missing from the deposit: `not covered`.
DECLARE `Relief under s 71DD(2)` IS ONE OF
    `no relief: s 71DD does not apply`
    `no duty is payable`
    `a reduction under s 71DD(7), whose formula is missing`
    `the relief the original contract would have qualified for (s 71DD(9a)), which is not encoded`

GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
GIVETH A `Relief under s 71DD(2)`
`the relief under s 71DD(2)` MEANS
    IF `s 71DD(9a) gives the conveyance the original contract's relief` `p`
    THEN `the relief the original contract would have qualified for (s 71DD(9a)), which is not encoded`
    ELSE IF (NOT (`s 71DD applies to the conveyance (s 71DD(1), (8), (9))` `p`))
         THEN `no relief: s 71DD does not apply`
         ELSE IF (`p`'s `the date the contract was entered into`) `is on or after` `the day the relief became nil duty at any value (s 71DD(2)(b))`
              THEN `no duty is payable`
              ELSE CONSIDER `p`'s `what is bought`
                   WHEN `a new home` THEN
                       IF `p`'s `the market value when the contract was entered into` AT MOST 650000
                       THEN `no duty is payable`
                       ELSE `a reduction under s 71DD(7), whose formula is missing`
                   OTHERWISE
                       IF `p`'s `the market value when the contract was entered into` AT MOST 400000
                       THEN `no duty is payable`
                       ELSE `a reduction under s 71DD(7), whose formula is missing`

GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
      `the duty otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relief under s 71DD(2)` `p`
    WHEN `no relief: s 71DD does not apply` THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` `the duty otherwise payable`
    WHEN `no duty is payable` THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
    WHEN `a reduction under s 71DD(7), whose formula is missing` THEN
        `not covered` `the s 71DD(7) formula for the reduction on a pre-6 June 2024 contract in the phase-out band is missing from the deposited text`
    WHEN `the relief the original contract would have qualified for (s 71DD(9a)), which is not encoded` THEN
        `not covered` `the s 71DD(9a) relief of the original contract turns on that contract's own facts and is not encoded`

§§ `s 71DB -- off-the-plan apartments (encoded only as to when it applies)`

-- s 71DB(1): "If on an application under this section ... the Commissioner is satisfied that the applicant is a
-- purchaser of a qualifying apartment under a qualifying off-the-plan contract, this section applies to a conveyance
-- under which the interest in the apartment is transferred to the applicant." (7): "qualifying off-the-plan contract
-- means a contract for the purchase of an apartment entered into between the prescribed date and 19 June 2016 (both
-- dates inclusive) or between 20 June 2016 and 30 June 2017 (both dates inclusive)" where the building is yet to be
-- built or substantially completed, or is to be substantially refurbished. (2) and (3) then set the duty: nil, or the
-- duty less a fixed or stage-dependent sum, or duty on a "dutiable value" whose (3)(a) formula is missing from the
-- deposit. None of that is encoded, so where s 71DB applies the duty answers `not covered`. The Commissioner's
-- satisfaction is a fact; no contract after 30 June 2017 can qualify. s 71DB and s 71DD never meet: s 71DD needs a
-- contract on or after 15 June 2023 (s 71DD(3)(a)).
`the last day of a qualifying off-the-plan contract (s 71DB(7))` MEANS YearMonthDay 2017 6 30

GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the purchase is of a qualifying apartment under a qualifying off-the-plan contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 71DB applies to the conveyance (s 71DB(1), (7))` IF
        ((`p`'s `the date the contract was entered into`) `is on or before` `the last day of a qualifying off-the-plan contract (s 71DB(7))`)
    AND `the Commissioner is satisfied the purchase is of a qualifying apartment under a qualifying off-the-plan contract`

-- The duty on the conveyance of a home after the concessions this encoding reaches: s 71DB (`not covered` where it
-- applies), then s 71DD.
GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
      `the duty otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the purchase is of a qualifying apartment under a qualifying off-the-plan contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the conveyance duty after the s 71DB and s 71DD concessions` MEANS
    IF `s 71DB applies to the conveyance (s 71DB(1), (7))` `p` `the Commissioner is satisfied the purchase is of a qualifying apartment under a qualifying off-the-plan contract`
    THEN `not covered` `s 71DB (off-the-plan apartments, contracts up to 30 June 2017) is not encoded, and its s 71DB(3)(a) dutiable value formula is missing from the deposited text`
    ELSE `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` `p` `the duty otherwise payable`

-- s 71DD(11a): "This section does not operate to provide relief from the foreign ownership surcharge (within the meaning
-- of section 72) payable on a contract ... entered into on or after the relevant day." s 72(4): the surcharge "is to be
-- taken for the purposes of this Act to be duty payable on the instrument". READING (NOTES.md, finding 4): on a contract
-- before the relevant day, "no duty will be payable" under s 71DD(2) reaches the surcharge too.
GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 71DD relief extends to the foreign ownership surcharge` IF
        (CONSIDER `the relief under s 71DD(2)` `p`
         WHEN `no duty is payable` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND ((`p`'s `the date the contract was entered into`) `is before` (`p`'s `the relevant day`))

§§ `s 71DD(4), (5) -- the residence requirement`

-- s 71DD(4): "(a) in the case of the conveyance or transfer of land on which a new home is situated -- the purchasers under
-- the contract must occupy the home as their principal place of residence for a continuous period of at least 6 months
-- (or a shorter period approved by the Commissioner) (the residence period) that commences within 12 months of the date
-- on which the conveyance or transfer occurs (the completion period); (b) in the case of ... vacant land on which a home
-- is to be built -- the purchasers ... must occupy a home on the land as their principal place of residence for a
-- continuous period of at least 6 months (or a shorter period approved by the Commissioner) (the residence period) that
-- commences before whichever of the following dates occurs first: (i) the date falling 12 months after the date on which
-- the purchaser was lawfully first able to use a home constructed on the land as a place of residence; (ii) the date
-- falling 36 months after the date on which the conveyance or transfer occurred". (5)(b): the Commissioner may "vary a
-- purchaser's required residence period at any time ... by approving a shorter residence period or a longer completion
-- period (or both)". READING (NOTES.md, finding 14): "within 12 months of" includes the anniversary; "commences before"
-- the (b) date means the day before it at the latest. An approved longer completion period is taken as months from the
-- transfer, and moves the last day only later.
`the residence period, in months (s 71DD(4))` MEANS 6

GIVEN `the date of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `a home on the land can now lawfully be used as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date a home on the land was first lawfully usable as a residence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to begin the residence period on vacant land (s 71DD(4)(b))` MEANS
    `days after` (0 MINUS 1) `the earlier date`
    WHERE
        `thirty-six months after the transfer` MEANS `months after` 36 `the date of the transfer`
        `the earlier date` MEANS
            IF `a home on the land can now lawfully be used as a place of residence`
            THEN `the earlier of` (`months after` 12 `the date a home on the land was first lawfully usable as a residence`) `and` `thirty-six months after the transfer`
            ELSE `thirty-six months after the transfer`

GIVEN `what is bought` IS A `What is bought`
      `the date of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `a home on the land can now lawfully be used as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date a home on the land was first lawfully usable as a residence` IS A DATE
      `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner, in months from the transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to begin the residence period (s 71DD(4), (5))` MEANS
    IF `approved` GREATER THAN 0 AND (`the day under (4)` `is before` (`months after` `approved` `the date of the transfer`))
    THEN `months after` `approved` `the date of the transfer`
    ELSE `the day under (4)`
    WHERE
        `approved` MEANS `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner, in months from the transfer`
        `the day under (4)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what is bought`
            WHEN `vacant land on which a home is to be built` THEN
                `the last day to begin the residence period on vacant land (s 71DD(4)(b))` `the date of the transfer` `a home on the land can now lawfully be used as a place of residence` `the date a home on the land was first lawfully usable as a residence`
            OTHERWISE `months after` 12 `the date of the transfer`

GIVEN `the day the purchasers began to occupy` IS A DATE
      `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the residence period ends (s 71DD(4), (5))` MEANS
    `months after` `months` `the day the purchasers began to occupy`
    WHERE
        `months` MEANS
            IF `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN `the lesser of` `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months` `the residence period, in months (s 71DD(4))`
            ELSE `the residence period, in months (s 71DD(4))`

§§ `s 71DE -- duty payable if the relief ceases to be available`

-- s 71DE(1): if relief was provided under s 71DD and "(i) the Commissioner ceases to be satisfied that the conveyance or
-- transfer qualifies for relief ...; or (ii) a purchaser ... fails to comply with a requirement under section 71DD(4),
-- section 71DD will cease to apply ... and duty will be payable ... as if no exemption or reduction in duty applied."
-- (2): "(a) the Commissioner must advise the purchasers in writing that relief from duty is no longer available ...;
-- (b) duty will be payable ... from the date on which the conveyance or transfer occurred; (c) the liability ... is to be
-- assessed in relation to the circumstances applying at the date of the conveyance ...; (d) the duty ... is to be
-- calculated according to the rates in force as at the date on which the conveyance or transfer occurred; (e) for the
-- purposes of section 20, the duty is to be regarded as having become chargeable on the conveyance or transfer in
-- consequence of section 71DD having ceased to apply ...; (f) the purchasers may, at the discretion of the Commissioner,
-- be liable to pay interest and penalty tax as if the failure to pay duty, or to pay full duty, at the date of the
-- conveyance or transfer were a tax default under the Taxation Administration Act 1996."
-- The rates in force at the transfer date are those of the deposited Schedule 2 (as at 2025-02-13); a later change to
-- the scale is not in the deposit.
GIVEN `the value of the property conveyed, at the date of the transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty payable when the relief ceases (s 71DE(1), (2)(c), (d))` MEANS
    `the conveyance duty on the general scale` `the value of the property conveyed, at the date of the transfer`

-- s 71DE(2)(f) with TAA ss 25-27, 30-32: interest runs as if the duty had been unpaid since the date of the transfer.
-- READING (NOTES.md, finding 17): the days counted are from the date of the transfer to the day of payment.
GIVEN `the duty` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner exercises the s 71DE(2)(f) discretion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days from the transfer to payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the market rate, per cent a year` IS A NUMBER
      `the default` IS A `Kind of tax default`
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it was not deliberate and reasonable care was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct` IS A `Taxpayer conduct`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most interest and penalty tax when the relief ceases (s 71DE(2)(f))` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner exercises the s 71DE(2)(f) discretion`
    THEN     `the interest on a tax default` `the duty` `the days from the transfer to payment` `the market rate, per cent a year`
        PLUS `the most penalty tax on a tax default` `the duty` `the default` `the Commissioner is satisfied it was not deliberate and reasonable care was taken` `the conduct`
    ELSE 0

-- s 71DE(2)(a) and (e) with s 20(2), as a rule. Clock: days from the event that ends the relief. `the days to pay` is
-- the count of days to two months after that event.
GIVEN `the days to pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
`s 71DE -- the relief ceases: the Commissioner advises, and the duty is paid within two months` MEANS
        (PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `advise the purchasers in writing that relief from duty is no longer available`)
    RAND
        (PARTY  `the purchasers`
         MUST   `pay the duty and have the instrument stamped`
         WITHIN `the days to pay`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the purchasers` BECAUSE "s 71DE(2)(e), s 20(2), (4): the duty became chargeable when the s 71DD relief ceased and must be paid within two months after that event; not stamped in time, an offence with a maximum penalty of $10 000; interest and penalty tax from the date of the transfer at the Commissioner's discretion (s 71DE(2)(f))")

-- s 71DD(4) with s 71DE, as a rule. Clock: days from the date of the transfer. `who must comply` is `the purchasers`, or
-- `a complying purchaser, the others exempted by the Commissioner` where s 71DD(5)(a) applies ("there are 2 or more
-- purchasers ...; at least 1 of the purchasers complies ...; and there are, in the Commissioner's opinion, good reasons to
-- exempt the non-complying purchaser"). Beginning to occupy late, or ceasing within the residence period, ends the
-- relief (s 71DE(1)(b)(ii)).
GIVEN `who must comply` IS A `Duty party`
      `the days to the last day to begin` IS A NUMBER
      `the days in the residence period` IS A NUMBER
      `the days to pay once the relief ceases` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 71DD(4) -- occupy the home for 6 months, or lose the relief under s 71DE` IS
    PARTY  `who must comply`
    MUST   `begin to occupy the home as principal place of residence`
    WITHIN `the days to the last day to begin`
    HENCE
        PARTY  `who must comply`
        SHANT  `cease to occupy the home as principal place of residence`
        WITHIN `the days in the residence period`
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   `s 71DE -- the relief ceases: the Commissioner advises, and the duty is paid within two months` `the days to pay once the relief ceases`
    LEST   `s 71DE -- the relief ceases: the Commissioner advises, and the duty is paid within two months` `the days to pay once the relief ceases`

§§ `s 2(14) and s 72 -- the foreign ownership surcharge`

-- s 2(14)(a): "a person is a foreign person if -- (i) in the case of a natural person -- the person is not -- (A) an
-- Australian citizen within the meaning of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007 of the Commonwealth; or (B) the holder of a
-- permanent visa within the meaning of section 30(1) of the Migration Act 1958 of the Commonwealth; or (C) a New Zealand
-- citizen who is the holder of a special category visa within the meaning of section 32(1) of the Migration Act 1958".
-- Corporations and trusts ((a)(ii), (b)-(d)) are NOT ENCODED.
GIVEN `the person is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the natural person is a foreign person (s 2(14)(a)(i))` IF
        (NOT `the person is an Australian citizen`)
    AND (NOT `the person holds a permanent visa`)
    AND (NOT `the person is a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa`)

-- s 72(1): "This section applies to a dutiable instrument ... executed, or taken to have been executed, on or after
-- 1 January 2018." (2): "If an instrument to which this section applies effects ... a transaction whereby an interest in
-- residential land is acquired by a foreign person or a person who takes the interest as trustee for a foreign trust, the
-- person is liable to pay a surcharge (a foreign ownership surcharge) to the Commissioner in addition to the duty payable
-- on the instrument." (3): "The amount of the foreign ownership surcharge is 7% of the value of the interest acquired by
-- the person in the residential land". (8): land is residential land if the Commissioner, after taking into account
-- information from the Valuer-General, so determines (a fact).
`the first day of the surcharge (s 72(1))` MEANS YearMonthDay 2018 1 1
`the surcharge rate, per cent (s 72(3))` MEANS 7

GIVEN `the date of execution` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner determines the land is residential land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acquiring is a foreign person, or trustee for a foreign trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the interest the person acquires` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the foreign ownership surcharge (s 72)` MEANS
    IF     (`the date of execution` `is on or after` `the first day of the surcharge (s 72(1))`)
       AND `the Commissioner determines the land is residential land`
       AND `the person acquiring is a foreign person, or trustee for a foreign trust`
    THEN `the value of the interest the person acquires` TIMES `the surcharge rate, per cent (s 72(3))` DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE 0

-- s 72(5): "If -- (a) a foreign ownership surcharge was paid by a person under this section because the person was a
-- foreign person when an interest in residential land was acquired by the person; and (b) the person ceases to be a
-- foreign person not more than 12 months after the acquisition of the interest; and (c) the person retains the interest
-- at the time that the person ceases to be a foreign person, the Commissioner must, on application by the person, refund
-- the amount of the foreign ownership surcharge to the person." READING: "not more than 12 months after" includes the
-- anniversary.
GIVEN `the surcharge was paid because the person was a foreign person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of acquisition` IS A DATE
      `the person has ceased to be a foreign person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person ceased to be a foreign person` IS A DATE
      `the person retained the interest at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surcharge must be refunded on application (s 72(5))` IF
        `the surcharge was paid because the person was a foreign person`
    AND `the person has ceased to be a foreign person`
    AND (`the date the person ceased to be a foreign person` `is on or before` (`months after` 12 `the date of acquisition`))
    AND `the person retained the interest at that time`

-- s 71DD(11a) and s 72 together: the surcharge on a home bought with the s 71DD relief claimed. On a contract before
-- the relevant day, the nil relief reaches the surcharge (READING, NOTES.md, finding 4). Where the relief on such a
-- contract is a s 71DD(7) reduction, whose formula is missing, or the original contract's under s 71DD(9a), whether and
-- how far it reaches the surcharge cannot be worked out, so the answer is `not covered` (finding 24). From the relevant
-- day, s 71DD(11a) leaves the surcharge in full.
GIVEN `p` IS A `New home purchase`
      `the date of execution` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner determines the land is residential land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acquiring is a foreign person, or trustee for a foreign trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the interest the person acquires` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the foreign ownership surcharge after any s 71DD relief (ss 71DD(11a), 72)` MEANS
    IF `the s 72 amount` EQUALS 0 OR `the s 71DD relief extends to the foreign ownership surcharge` `p`
    THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
    ELSE IF (`p`'s `the date the contract was entered into`) `is before` (`p`'s `the relevant day`)
         THEN CONSIDER `the relief under s 71DD(2)` `p`
              WHEN `a reduction under s 71DD(7), whose formula is missing` THEN
                  `not covered` `the s 71DD(7) formula for the reduction on a pre-6 June 2024 contract in the phase-out band is missing from the deposited text`
              WHEN `the relief the original contract would have qualified for (s 71DD(9a)), which is not encoded` THEN
                  `not covered` `the s 71DD(9a) relief of the original contract turns on that contract's own facts and is not encoded`
              OTHERWISE `the amount, in dollars, is` `the s 72 amount`
         ELSE `the amount, in dollars, is` `the s 72 amount`
    WHERE
        `the s 72 amount` MEANS
            `the foreign ownership surcharge (s 72)` `the date of execution` `the Commissioner determines the land is residential land` `the person acquiring is a foreign person, or trustee for a foreign trust` `the value of the interest the person acquires`

-- The refund as a rule. Applying is the person's choice and no time is set for it, nor for the refund (no WITHIN).
GIVEN `the refund conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 72(5) -- on application, the Commissioner must refund the surcharge` IS
    IF `the refund conditions are met`
    THEN PARTY `the person who paid the surcharge`
         DO    `apply for a refund of the foreign ownership surcharge`
         HENCE (PARTY `the Commissioner`
                MUST  `refund the foreign ownership surcharge`)
         LEST  FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
